      ],
      "message": "btcsignals: Use StdMutex so a signal can deliver log entries\n\nLocking a sync.h Mutex can log: with DEBUG_LOCKCONTENTION it logs lock\ncontention, and with DEBUG_LOCKORDER it logs lock order errors. A signal\nthat delivers kernel log entries, as the next commit adds, would then\nlock its own mutex again on the same thread while delivering that entry,\nand deadlock. Use a StdMutex, as Logger in logging.h does for the same\nreason.\n\nThe mutex only guards the connection list and is never held while\ncallbacks run, so lock order checking adds little here.\n\nThis change was written with Claude Opus 5.5.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Ryan Ofsky",
