      "message": "kernel: Dispatch log callbacks with btcsignals so they run without the logger mutex\n\nKernelLogger called log callbacks while holding its mutex, so a callback\nthat logged, or destroyed a kernel object that logs, deadlocked. A\ngarbage collector running finalizers inside a callback can trigger this\n(https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34775#issuecomment-6278257737).\n\nDeliver entries through a btcsignals::signal instead, which holds no lock\nwhile callbacks run. The API is unchanged. Behavior changes:\n\n- Callbacks can run on several threads at the same time, so they must be\n  thread-safe.\n- Callbacks may call kernel functions, including creating and destroying\n  logging connections, their own included.\n- Destroying a connection no longer waits for invocations already\n  running on other threads. The user data is destroyed when the last one\n  returns, as with other btcsignals users.\n\nThis is the follow-up suggested in\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34374#discussion_r4034240501.\n\nThis change was written with Claude Opus 5.5.",
